// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// © antonametov88
//
// Forward Range Cone — a volatility cone drawn from the CURRENT price forward,
// and nothing else. Derived from range-projection.pine (Quarterly StdDev Fan):
// same sigma estimator, different question. The fan answers "how far has price
// wandered from the quarter's open"; this answers "from where price is now, how
// far could it go over the next N calendar days".
//
// WHAT THIS COMPUTES:
// On the last bar only, from anchor price P0 at anchor time t0, for k = 1 and 2:
//     P0 * exp(+k * sigma_Q * sqrt(h / 91.3125))   and   P0 * exp(-k * sigma_Q * sqrt(h / 91.3125))
// where h is CALENDAR days after t0, out to the input "Horizon (calendar days)".
// 91.3125 = 365.25 / 4 is the mean length of a calendar quarter in days, so the
// cone is exactly +/-k sigma_Q wide one mean quarter out. The cone is a polyline
// sampled uniformly in sqrt(h). Labels give the +/-1 and +/-2 sigma prices at the
// horizon with their percent distance from P0. The status cell gives sigma_Q, the
// quarter window it came from, the anchor, and the same levels at the chosen
// horizon and at 7, 30 and 91 days.
//     sigma_Q = mean over L COMPLETED quarters of ln(H_j / L_j)  /  sqrt(8 / pi)
// H_j and L_j are the high and low of TradingView's own 3M bar. Requirements (else
// n/a, never a substitute value): L consecutive quarters, none of them the symbol's
// first (inception, possibly partial) 3M bar, every high/low valid, non-zero range.
// Nothing is plotted on historical bars: there are no plot() calls.
//
// WHICH QUARTERS ARE IN THE WINDOW:
// One request returns the 3M bar visible on the last chart bar and the 3M bar
// before it. The visible one is used only if its calendar quarter had ended by the
// reference time (the bar's close time if the bar is confirmed, its open time if it
// is still forming); otherwise the one before it is used, which is always a
// finished 3M bar. So a developing quarter never enters the window. Consequences,
// both visible in the status cell's window text:
//   - after the last session of a quarter and before the first bar of the next,
//     the just-finished quarter is not yet in the window;
//   - on a forming weekly bar that spans a quarter boundary, before the new
//     quarter's first session, the window ends at q-2 for those days.
//
// ANCHOR (input "Anchor"):
//   - "Last closed bar" (default): P0 = close of the most recent CONFIRMED bar,
//     t0 = that bar's time_close. While a bar is forming the cone stays put and the
//     forming bar is seen moving inside it.
//   - "Live price": P0 = the forming bar's current close, t0 = now (clamped to the
//     bar). The cone moves with every tick. That is the point of the mode, and it
//     is the one place this script is not fixed between ticks.
//
// SOURCE:
//   - Range constant: Feller, W. (1951), "The asymptotic distribution of the
//     range of sums of independent random variables", Annals of Mathematical
//     Statistics 22(3), 427-432 — expected range of a Brownian path over unit
//     time = sqrt(8/pi) * sigma.
//   - Range-based sigma: Parkinson, M. (1980), "The Extreme Value Method for
//     Estimating the Variance of the Rate of Return", Journal of Business 53(1),
//     61-65, first moment E[ln(H/L)] = sqrt(8/pi) * sigma. Parkinson's published
//     estimator uses the SECOND moment; this script uses the first-moment form
//     (a judgement, carried over from range-projection.pine).
//   - sqrt(t) scaling of a log-normal price: textbook (e.g. Hull, Options, Futures
//     and Other Derivatives, lognormal property of stock prices).
//   - THE CONE AS A WHOLE IS AN ORIGINAL CONSTRUCTION for this trader. No published
//     indicator is reproduced.
//
// ASSUMPTIONS AND KNOWN BIASES — READ BEFORE TRUSTING A LEVEL:
//   - Driftless Brownian motion in log price with constant volatility. Real tails
//     are fatter: +/-1 and +/-2 sigma will NOT contain 68.3% and 95.4% of outcomes.
//     It is a volatility envelope, not a forecast, and it has no direction.
//   - sigma_Q is SLOW: it is an average over L whole quarters (default 8 = two
//     years) and does not react to the current volatility regime. In a calm market
//     after a turbulent two years the cone is too wide; in a fresh sell-off it is
//     too narrow. No short-window estimator is offered here; adding one is a
//     separate, sourced decision.
//   - A quarterly sigma is scaled DOWN to days by sqrt(time). Short-horizon levels
//     (a few days) assume volatility is the same at every scale, which it is not.
//   - h is calendar time: weekends and holidays count as elapsed time. Over a
//     horizon of a few days this misstates the width (a 3-day horizon across a
//     weekend holds one session, not three).
//   - H/L of a 3M bar miss extremes outside recorded trading; drift biases the
//     range slightly high (see range-projection.pine header for the figures).
//   - Unsupported (shown as n/a, nothing computed): timeframe above 3M, and
//     non-standard chart types (Renko, Kagi, Line Break, Point and Figure, Range,
//     Heikin Ashi, tick charts). Futures and other symbols whose bars open on the
//     previous calendar day are outside the intended ETF/stock scope.
//
// REPAINT: no historical value is plotted, so nothing historical can move. In
// "Last closed bar" mode the cone is a function of confirmed data only (confirmed
// close, completed 3M bars read with lookahead_off) and is redrawn identically on
// every tick. In "Live price" mode the cone follows the forming bar by design.
//
// COMPILE CHECK: NOT RUN. This file was written on 2026-11-23 and has not been
// pasted into TradingView's editor. Nothing below has been observed:
//   - that it compiles at all;
//   - which 3M set (visible or previous) is selected on a daily, weekly and
//     intraday chart, in session and out of session;
//   - that xloc.bar_time points beyond the last bar render where expected, and
//     where a point at t0 inside the last bar lands;
//   - whether a weekly bar's time_close is the Friday close or the next Monday
//     00:00 (it only moves the cone's start by a weekend);
//   - no hand-computed sigma_Q has been compared with the status cell, and the
//     status cell has not been compared with range-projection.pine's on the same
//     symbol (they should agree whenever both name the same window).
//@version=6
indicator("Forward Range Cone", shorttitle="RangeCone", overlay=true,
     max_labels_count=10, max_polylines_count=10)

// ===== CONSTANTS =====
// Expected range of a standard Brownian motion over unit time (Feller 1951).
float K_RANGE = math.sqrt(8.0 / math.pi)
// Mean calendar quarter in days (365.25 / 4): the time unit of sigma_Q.
float Q_DAYS  = 91.3125
int   MS_DAY  = 86400000
// Polyline segments (uniform in sqrt(h); chord error <= 1/(4*M) of k*sigma_h).
int   M_SEG   = 32
color C_LINE2 = color.new(#aaaacc, 50)

// ===== INPUTS =====
int    i_lookback = input.int(8, "Lookback Quarters", minval=4, maxval=20, group="Cone",
     tooltip="Completed calendar quarters in the sigma window. Relative standard error of sigma is about 30%/sqrt(L): 10.5% at 8, 15% at 4.")
int    i_days     = input.int(30, "Horizon (calendar days)", minval=1, maxval=365, group="Cone",
     tooltip="How far ahead the cone is drawn. Calendar days, weekends included. Width at the horizon is sigma_Q * sqrt(days / 91.3125).")
string ANCHOR_CLOSED = "Last closed bar"
string ANCHOR_LIVE   = "Live price"
string i_anchor   = input.string(ANCHOR_CLOSED, "Anchor", options=[ANCHOR_CLOSED, ANCHOR_LIVE], group="Cone",
     tooltip="Last closed bar: the cone starts at the most recent confirmed close and does not move while a bar forms. Live price: it starts at the current price and moves with every tick.")
bool   i_labels   = input.bool(true, "Show Labels", group="Display")
color  i_c1       = input.color(color.new(#00c87a, 65), "±1σ Color", group="Display")
color  i_c2       = input.color(color.new(#1a2a44, 75), "±2σ Color", group="Display")
color  i_cmid     = input.color(color.new(#ffffff, 30), "Midline", group="Display")

// ===== HELPERS =====
// Quarter id of a timestamp: 4*year + quarter index (0..3), in timezone tz.
f_qid(int t, string tz) =>
    4 * year(t, tz) + math.floor((month(t, tz) - 1) / 3)

// 00:00 on the first day of quarter qid, exchange timezone.
f_qstart(int qid) =>
    timestamp(syminfo.timezone, math.floor(qid / 4), 3 * (qid % 4) + 1, 1, 0, 0, 0)

f_qlabel(int qid) =>
    str.tostring(math.floor(qid / 4)) + "Q" + str.tostring(qid % 4 + 1)

// Evaluated in the 3M context (called from request.security). Identical to
// range-projection.pine. Returns [quarter id of this 3M bar, mean ln(H/L) over the
// last len bars or na (na unless code 0), validity code, 0-based 3M bar index],
// then the same four values as they were on the previous 3M bar.
// Codes: 0 ok; 1 fewer than len post-inception bars; 3 a quarter missing inside
// the window; 4 invalid high/low in the window; 5 zero range.
f_htf(int len) =>
    float rng    = (high > 0 and low > 0 and high >= low) ? math.log(high / low) : na
    float good   = ta.sma(na(rng) ? 0.0 : 1.0, len)
    float mean_r = ta.sma(rng, len)
    int   qid    = f_qid(time, syminfo.timezone)
    int   span   = qid - qid[len - 1]
    int   code   = 0
    if bar_index < len
        code := 1
    else if na(span) or span != len - 1
        code := 3
    else if na(good) or good < 1.0
        code := 4
    else if na(mean_r) or not (mean_r > 0)
        code := 5
    float val    = code == 0 ? mean_r : na
    int   qid_1  = qid[1]
    float val_1  = val[1]
    int   code_1 = code[1]
    int   idx_1  = bar_index[1]
    [qid, val, code, bar_index, qid_1, val_1, code_1, idx_1]

f_reason(int c, int have, int len) =>
    string s = "quarterly data unavailable"
    if c == 1
        s := "need " + str.tostring(len) + " completed quarters, have " + str.tostring(have)
    else if c == 2
        s := "no completed quarter in the quarterly data"
    else if c == 3
        s := "a quarter is missing inside the sigma window"
    else if c == 4
        s := "invalid high/low in the sigma window"
    else if c == 5
        s := "zero range"
    else if c == 6
        s := "anchor price missing"
    s

// Price at k-sigma distance w (log units) from p.
f_lvl(float p, float w) =>
    str.tostring(p * math.exp(w), format.mintick)

f_pct(float w) =>
    float pc = (math.exp(w) - 1.0) * 100.0
    (pc >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pc, "#.0") + "%"

// One status-cell row: +/-1 and +/-2 sigma price ranges d calendar days out.
f_row(int d, float p, float sq) =>
    float w = sq * math.sqrt(d / Q_DAYS)
    str.tostring(d) + "d   ±1σ " + f_lvl(p, -w) + " – " + f_lvl(p, w) + "   ±2σ " + f_lvl(p, -2.0 * w) + " – " + f_lvl(p, 2.0 * w)

// Closed polygon between two point lists (top forward, bottom reversed).
f_region(array<chart.point> top, array<chart.point> bot) =>
    array<chart.point> r = array.copy(top)
    for i = array.size(bot) - 1 to 0
        array.push(r, array.get(bot, i))
    r

// ===== CHART SUPPORT =====
// Standard time-based charts, timeframe <= 3M. Anything else: n/a, nothing computed.
bool   tf_ok  = chart.is_standard and not timeframe.isticks and timeframe.in_seconds() <= timeframe.in_seconds("3M")
// On an unsupported chart the request is pointed at the chart's own timeframe and
// its result is never read.
string htf_tf = tf_ok ? "3M" : timeframe.period

// ===== QUARTERLY SIGMA DATA (3M context) =====
[hq_qid, hq_mean, hq_code, hq_idx, hq_qid1, hq_mean1, hq_code1, hq_idx1] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htf_tf, f_htf(i_lookback),
     gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

// Previous bar's close and close time (history references kept at global scope).
float close_1 = close[1]
int   tclose_1 = time_close[1]

// ===== CONE, LABELS, STATUS (last bar only) =====
var array<polyline> cone_poly = array.new<polyline>()
var array<label>    cone_lbl  = array.new<label>()
var table           tbl       = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 1, border_width=1)

if barstate.islast
    // Delete-then-create on every tick.
    while array.size(cone_poly) > 0
        polyline.delete(array.pop(cone_poly))
    while array.size(cone_lbl) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(cone_lbl))

    // ----- sigma: the newest 3M set whose quarter is over -----
    // Reference time: the bar's close if the bar is confirmed, else its open.
    int   t_ref  = barstate.isconfirmed ? time_close : time
    int   code   = 2
    float s_mean = na
    int   s_idx  = na
    int   s_qid  = na
    if tf_ok
        bool cur_done = false
        if not na(hq_qid) and not na(hq_code)
            cur_done := f_qstart(hq_qid + 1) <= t_ref
        if cur_done
            code   := hq_code
            s_mean := hq_mean
            s_idx  := hq_idx
            s_qid  := hq_qid
        else if not na(hq_qid1) and not na(hq_code1)
            // The 3M bar before the visible one is always a finished bar.
            code   := hq_code1
            s_mean := hq_mean1
            s_idx  := hq_idx1
            s_qid  := hq_qid1
    if code == 0 and (na(s_mean) or not (s_mean > 0))
        code := 4

    // ----- anchor -----
    bool  use_cur = i_anchor == ANCHOR_LIVE or barstate.isconfirmed
    float p0 = use_cur ? close : close_1
    int   t0 = na
    if use_cur
        t0 := barstate.isconfirmed ? time_close : math.max(time, math.min(timenow, time_close))
    else
        t0 := tclose_1
    if code == 0 and (na(p0) or not (p0 > 0) or na(t0))
        code := 6

    float sig = code == 0 ? s_mean / K_RANGE : na

    if code == 0
        float w_h  = sig * math.sqrt(i_days / Q_DAYS)
        int   h_ms = i_days * MS_DAY
        array<chart.point> pu2 = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pu1 = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pm0 = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pd1 = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pd2 = array.new<chart.point>()
        // s = sqrt(fraction of the horizon elapsed), uniform steps.
        for j = 0 to M_SEG
            float s  = j * 1.0 / M_SEG
            int   tx = t0 + math.round(s * s * h_ms)
            float wj = w_h * s
            array.push(pu2, chart.point.from_time(tx, p0 * math.exp(2.0 * wj)))
            array.push(pu1, chart.point.from_time(tx, p0 * math.exp(wj)))
            array.push(pm0, chart.point.from_time(tx, p0))
            array.push(pd1, chart.point.from_time(tx, p0 * math.exp(-wj)))
            array.push(pd2, chart.point.from_time(tx, p0 * math.exp(-2.0 * wj)))

        // Fills first, lines on top.
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(f_region(pu2, pu1), closed=true, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=color(na), fill_color=i_c2))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(f_region(pu1, pd1), closed=true, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=color(na), fill_color=i_c1))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(f_region(pd1, pd2), closed=true, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=color(na), fill_color=i_c2))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(pu2, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=C_LINE2, line_width=1))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(pu1, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=color.new(i_c1, 10), line_width=1))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(pm0, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=i_cmid, line_width=1, line_style=line.style_dashed))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(pd1, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=color.new(i_c1, 10), line_width=1))
        array.push(cone_poly, polyline.new(pd2, xloc=xloc.bar_time, line_color=C_LINE2, line_width=1))

        if i_labels
            int xe = t0 + h_ms
            array.push(cone_lbl, label.new(x=xe, y=p0 * math.exp(2.0 * w_h), text="+2σ " + f_lvl(p0, 2.0 * w_h) + " (" + f_pct(2.0 * w_h) + ")", xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(i_c2, 10), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small))
            array.push(cone_lbl, label.new(x=xe, y=p0 * math.exp(w_h), text="+1σ " + f_lvl(p0, w_h) + " (" + f_pct(w_h) + ")", xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(i_c1, 10), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small))
            array.push(cone_lbl, label.new(x=xe, y=p0 * math.exp(-w_h), text="-1σ " + f_lvl(p0, -w_h) + " (" + f_pct(-w_h) + ")", xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(i_c1, 10), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small))
            array.push(cone_lbl, label.new(x=xe, y=p0 * math.exp(-2.0 * w_h), text="-2σ " + f_lvl(p0, -2.0 * w_h) + " (" + f_pct(-2.0 * w_h) + ")", xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(i_c2, 10), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small))

    // Status cell: always present; "n/a — reason" on every unavailable case.
    string st    = ""
    color  st_bg = color.new(color.gray, 70)
    if not tf_ok
        st := "n/a — unsupported chart (needs a standard time-based chart, timeframe 3M or shorter)"
    else if code != 0
        st := "n/a — " + f_reason(code, s_idx, i_lookback)
    else
        st := "σQ " + str.tostring(sig * 100.0, "#.00") + "%  (L=" + str.tostring(i_lookback) + ", " + f_qlabel(s_qid - i_lookback + 1) + " to " + f_qlabel(s_qid) + ")\n" +
             "from " + str.tostring(p0, format.mintick) + "  (" + (use_cur and not barstate.isconfirmed ? "live, " : "close, ") + str.format_time(t0, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", syminfo.timezone) + ")\n" +
             f_row(i_days, p0, sig) + "  ← cone"
        if i_days != 7
            st += "\n" + f_row(7, p0, sig)
        if i_days != 30
            st += "\n" + f_row(30, p0, sig)
        if i_days != 91
            st += "\n" + f_row(91, p0, sig)
        st_bg := color.new(color.black, 40)
    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, st, text_color=color.white, bgcolor=st_bg, text_halign=text.align_left, text_size=size.small)
